				<div id="bodyContent" class="vector-body" aria-labelledby="firstHeading" data-mw-ve-target-container>
					<div class="vector-body-before-content">
							<div class="mw-indicators">
		</div>

						<div id="siteSub" class="noprint">From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</div>
					</div>
					<div id="contentSub"><div id="mw-content-subtitle"></div></div>
					
					
					<div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-body-content"><div class="mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang="en" dir="ltr" data-mw-parsoid-version="0.24.0.0-alpha18" data-mw-html-version="2.8.0"><section data-mw-section-id="0" id="mwAQ"><div class="shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux" style="display:none" about="#mwt1" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"short description","href":"./Template:Short_description"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Classifies holomorphic vector bundles over the complex projective line"}},"i":0}}]}'>Classifies holomorphic vector bundles over the complex projective line</div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_short_description"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Short_description_matches_Wikidata"/></span>
<p id="mwAw">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematics" title="Mathematics" id="mwBA">mathematics</a>, the <b id="mwBQ">Birkhoff–Grothendieck theorem</b> classifies <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holomorphic_vector_bundle" title="Holomorphic vector bundle" id="mwBg">holomorphic</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vector_bundle" title="Vector bundle" id="mwBw">vector bundles</a> over the complex <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Projective_line" title="Projective line" id="mwCA">projective line</a>. In particular every holomorphic vector bundle over <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt4" id="mwCQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":" \\mathbb{CP}^1 "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {CP} ^{1}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">C</mi>
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {CP} ^{1}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/82c98c461bccbd4567716df0a6a2ff97bf9371af" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:4.153ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {CP} ^{1}}"/></span> is a direct sum of holomorphic <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Line_bundle" title="Line bundle" id="mwCg">line bundles</a>. The theorem was proved by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Grothendieck" title="Alexander Grothendieck" about="#mwt2" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"harvs","href":"./Template:Harvs"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"txt"},"last":{"wt":"Grothendieck"},"first":{"wt":"Alexander"},"authorlink":{"wt":"Alexander Grothendieck"},"year":{"wt":"1957"},"loc":{"wt":"Theorem 2.1"}},"i":0}}]}'>Alexander<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Grothendieck</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt2"> </span><span about="#mwt2">(</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#CITEREFGrothendieck1957" about="#mwt2" class="mw-selflink-fragment">1957</a><span about="#mwt2">,</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt2"> </span><span about="#mwt2">Theorem 2.1)</span>,<sup about="#mwt7" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-1" id="mwDA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDw">]</span></span></a></sup> and is more or less equivalent to  <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birkhoff_factorization" title="Birkhoff factorization" id="mwEA">Birkhoff factorization</a> introduced by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_David_Birkhoff" title="George David Birkhoff" about="#mwt3" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"harvs","href":"./Template:Harvs"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"txt"},"last":{"wt":"Birkhoff"},"first":{"wt":"George David"},"year":{"wt":"1909"},"authorlink":{"wt":"George David Birkhoff"}},"i":0}}]}'>George David<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Birkhoff</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt3"> </span><span about="#mwt3">(</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#CITEREFBirkhoff1909" about="#mwt3" class="mw-selflink-fragment">1909</a><span about="#mwt3">)</span>.<sup about="#mwt10" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-2" id="mwEg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFA">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwFg" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwFw" aria-labelledby="Statement"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Statement">Statement</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Birkhoff%E2%80%93Grothendieck_theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: Statement"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwGA">More precisely, the statement of the theorem is as the following.</p>

<p id="mwGQ">Every <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holomorphic_vector_bundle" title="Holomorphic vector bundle" id="mwGg">holomorphic vector bundle</a> <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt11" id="mwGw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":" \\mathcal{E} "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle {\mathcal {E}}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi class="MJX-tex-caligraphic" mathvariant="script">E</mi>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle {\mathcal {E}}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/9c298ed828ff778065aeb5f0f305097f55bb9ae0" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.311ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\mathcal {E}}}"/></span> on <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt12" id="mwHA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":" \\mathbb{CP}^1 "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {CP} ^{1}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">C</mi>
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {CP} ^{1}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/82c98c461bccbd4567716df0a6a2ff97bf9371af" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:4.153ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {CP} ^{1}}"/></span> is holomorphically isomorphic to a direct sum of line bundles:<sup about="#mwt13" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-3" id="mwHQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHw">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<dl id="mwIQ"><dd id="mwIg"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt14" id="mwIw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":" \\mathcal{E}\\cong\\mathcal{O}(a_1)\\oplus \\cdots \\oplus \\mathcal{O}(a_n)."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle {\mathcal {E}}\cong {\mathcal {O}}(a_{1})\oplus \cdots \oplus {\mathcal {O}}(a_{n}).}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi class="MJX-tex-caligraphic" mathvariant="script">E</mi>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
        <mo>≅<!-- ≅ --></mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi class="MJX-tex-caligraphic" mathvariant="script">O</mi>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <msub>
          <mi>a</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>⊕<!-- ⊕ --></mo>
        <mo>⋯<!-- ⋯ --></mo>
        <mo>⊕<!-- ⊕ --></mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi class="MJX-tex-caligraphic" mathvariant="script">O</mi>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <msub>
          <mi>a</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>.</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle {\mathcal {E}}\cong {\mathcal {O}}(a_{1})\oplus \cdots \oplus {\mathcal {O}}(a_{n}).}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/fff668cb442dba64217f91cf38d6210eb07930e2" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:25.511ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\mathcal {E}}\cong {\mathcal {O}}(a_{1})\oplus \cdots \oplus {\mathcal {O}}(a_{n}).}"/></span></dd></dl>

<p id="mwJA">The notation implies each summand is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serre_twist" title="Serre twist" class="mw-redirect" id="mwJQ">Serre twist</a> some number of times of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trivial_bundle" title="Trivial bundle" class="mw-redirect" id="mwJg">trivial bundle</a>. The representation is unique up to permuting factors.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwJw" aria-labelledby="Generalization"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Generalization">Generalization</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Birkhoff%E2%80%93Grothendieck_theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Generalization"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwKA">The same result holds in algebraic geometry for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algebraic_vector_bundle" title="Algebraic vector bundle" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKQ">algebraic vector bundle</a> over <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt15" id="mwKg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{P}^1_k"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} _{k}^{1}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>k</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} _{k}^{1}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/3d7de2a07b105f1791a49809f476ddcbf6c31af0" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:2.509ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} _{k}^{1}}"/></span> for any field <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt16" id="mwKw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"k"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle k}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>k</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle k}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/c3c9a2c7b599b37105512c5d570edc034056dd40" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.211ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle k}"/></span>.<sup about="#mwt19" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-4" id="mwLA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLg">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLw">]</span></span></a></sup>
It also holds for  <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt20" id="mwMA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{P}^1"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{1}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{1}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/5e38808c13ecc929e128079b70c1642554e2a4b3" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.475ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{1}}"/></span> with one or two orbifold points, and for chains of projective lines meeting along nodes.
<sup about="#mwt23" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-5" id="mwMQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMw">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwNQ" aria-labelledby="Applications"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Applications">Applications</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Birkhoff%E2%80%93Grothendieck_theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Applications"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwNg">One application of this theorem is it gives a classification of all coherent sheaves on <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt24" id="mwNw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{CP}^1"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {CP} ^{1}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">C</mi>
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {CP} ^{1}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/82c98c461bccbd4567716df0a6a2ff97bf9371af" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:4.153ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {CP} ^{1}}"/></span>. We have two cases, vector bundles and coherent sheaves supported along a subvariety, so <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt25" id="mwOA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathcal{O}(k), \\mathcal{O}_{nx}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle {\mathcal {O}}(k),{\mathcal {O}}_{nx}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi class="MJX-tex-caligraphic" mathvariant="script">O</mi>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>k</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <msub>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
              <mi class="MJX-tex-caligraphic" mathvariant="script">O</mi>
            </mrow>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
            <mi>x</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle {\mathcal {O}}(k),{\mathcal {O}}_{nx}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/41b2de520913224bb65dd4574e9be375e4b65b32" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:9.913ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\mathcal {O}}(k),{\mathcal {O}}_{nx}}"/></span> where n is the degree of the fat point at <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt26" id="mwOQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"x \\in \\mathbb{CP}^1"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle x\in \mathbb {CP} ^{1}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>x</mi>
        <mo>∈<!-- ∈ --></mo>
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">C</mi>
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle x\in \mathbb {CP} ^{1}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/30b6a743ba61bd5deec76ce2f36a33773f7f6440" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:8.323ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle x\in \mathbb {CP} ^{1}}"/></span>. Since the only subvarieties are points, we have a complete classification of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coherent_sheaf" title="Coherent sheaf" id="mwOg">coherent sheaves</a>.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwOw" aria-labelledby="See_also"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="See_also">See also</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Birkhoff%E2%80%93Grothendieck_theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: See also"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<ul id="mwPA"><li id="mwPQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algebraic_geometry_of_projective_spaces" title="Algebraic geometry of projective spaces" id="mwPg">Algebraic geometry of projective spaces</a></li>
<li id="mwPw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euler_sequence" title="Euler sequence" id="mwQA">Euler sequence</a></li>
<li id="mwQQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splitting_principle" title="Splitting principle" id="mwQg">Splitting principle</a></li>
<li id="mwQw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K-theory" title="K-theory" id="mwRA">K-theory</a></li>
<li id="mwRQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jumping_line" title="Jumping line" id="mwRg">Jumping line</a></li></ul>

